    "md5": "83f93bacb7b05cfca2787ff5ffb67b08",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2066,
    "chunk_text": "11. When the premises are not covered by a solid waste management service implemented by the Pradeshiya Sabha, the premises should be constructed in accordance with the recommendations of the Public Health Inspector or the Medical Officer of Health.\n\n13. Any Licensee who has received a Notice of such Section 12 of this by-law shall act in accordance with the notice as set forth in the Notice. The Chairman shall be entitled to extend the specified period of notice upon a reasonable written request by the Licensee. However, the extension period should not exceed 14 days.\n\n14. In the event that any licensee who has received a notice in terms of section 12 of this by-law has failed to act in the manner specified in that notice or before the date on which such notice is extended, the license issued to the relevant place shall be revoked by the Chairman. It must be legal.\n\n15. It is an offense to maintain premises without a license to be obtained under this by-law or to violate any of the provisions of the by-law and after being convicted by a court of competent jurisdiction for such offense, 122 of the Pradeshiya Sabha Act, No.15 of 1987 (2) Subject to a fine referred to in subsection (2). When a violation or violation is continued by a person who has been found guilty of an offense by a court of competent jurisdiction over the offense, a written notice shall be given by the Chairman or the Medical Officer of Health, Public Health Inspector. Each subsequent violation continues An additional fine of the above section shall also be imposed for a fine.\n\n16. Unless otherwise required in the by-laws.\n\n\"Chairman\" means the person holding the office of Chairman of this Pradeshiya Sabha or performing the functions of that office.\n\n43A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01