    "chunk_text": "98 A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\nGALIGAMUWA PRADESHIYA SABHA\n\nBy- Law Regarding Maintenance of Hotels\n\nBy-Law on the Maintenance of Hotels within the Authoritative Area of Galigamuwa Pradeshiya Sabha\n\n1. This By-Law is enacted to regulate, administer and control the operation of hotels within the area of authority of the Galigamuwa Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n2. This by-law is known as the by-law of operating a hotel within the area of the Galigamuwa pradeshiya sabha.\n\n3. (1) No person shall operate a hotel within the premises of the Galigamuwa Pradeshiya Sabha (hereinafter referred to as the Pradeshiya Sabha) unless there is a valid license issued by it to the Chairman.\n\n3. (2) Every person applying for a license under this by-law shall apply for a license under an application prepared in accordance with the first subsection herein.\n\n3. (3) The fees payable for a license under this section shall be the fees charged by the Council in accordance with the provisions of the Basic Law.\n\n4. (1) Any person who wishes to commence and maintain a premises subject to a permit under section 3(1) above shall have his prior approval under this by-law, unless the by-law is in force. There is no entitlement to apply for a license under section 3(2) of the Act.\n\n4. (2) The President shall approve the report of the Public Health Inspector and the Medical Officer of Health on a request for prior approval under this section.\n\n4. (3) The inspection fee to be paid under the approval of this section may be determined by the Council from time to time by a resolution of the resolution.\n\n5. Every person applying for a license under section 3(2) of this by-law must meet the following conditions:\n\n5. (1) Approval under Section 4(1) of the by-Law when the business is a start-up business."
  },
