    "chunk_size_bytes": 2022,
    "chunk_text": "THIS is to notify that I, Dhamma Dissanayake, Governor of the Sabaragamuwa Province has approved the by-law regarding the places where Animals Are Slaughter and Kept for Slaughter within authoritative area of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha, prepared by the Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha by virtue of powers vested in it under section 122 read with section 126 of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, No. 15 of 1987 and passed at its general meeting held on 09.07.2019, by virtue of powers vested under section 123(1) of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, read with section 2 of Provincial Council (Consequential Provisions) Act, No. 12 of 1989, and it will be effective within authoritative area of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha from the date this notification is published in the Gazette.\n\nDHAMMA DISSANAYAKE, Governor, Sabaragamuwa Province.\n\nAt the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council, On this 30th day of October, 2019.\n\n1.This By-law is enacted to regulate, administer and standardize the places where animals are slaughtered andkept for slaughter in Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area.\n\n2.This by-law is known as the by-law on the places where animals are slaughtered and kept for slaughter inYatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area.\n\n13A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\n3. (1) Any person within the premises of the Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha (hereinafter referred to as the premises of the Pradeshiya Sabha) shall have a valid license issued by it to the Chairman of the Pradeshiya Sabha. Non-animals (sometimes referred to herein as \"premature animals\") should not be kept for food and maintained in a slaughterhouse.\n\n3. (2) Any person who wishes to obtain a license under this by-law shall submit to the Chairman an application prepared in accordance with the form in the first schedule hereof."
  },
