    "md5": "0665075bdf3e4f3b83484cb5c35e5221",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1969,
    "chunk_text": "THIS is to notify that I, Dhamma Dissanayake, Governor of the Sabaragamuwa Province has approved the By-law regarding maintenance of Meat Stalls within authoritative area of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha, prepared by the Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha by virtue of powers vested in it under Section 122 read with Section 126 of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, No. 15 of 1987 and passed at its General meeting held on 09.07.2019, by virtue of powers vested under Section 123(1) of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, read with Section 2 of Provincial Council (Consequential Provisions) Act, No. 12 of 1989, and it will be effective within authoritative area of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha from the date this notification is published in the Gazette.\n\nDHAMMA DISSANAYAKE, Governor, Sabaragamuwa Province.\n\nBy-Law on the maintenance of Meat Stalls within the Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area\n\n1.This By-Law is enacted to regulate, administer and control the operation of meat outlets within the area of authority of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n2.This by-law is known as the by-law on the sale of meat in authoritative area of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\nBy law regarding meat stalls\n\n3.A Person who wishes to obtain a license pursuant to this by-law shall apply by an application prepared in accordance with the first schedule of this by law.\n\n3. (1) Where any person has a valid license issued by the Chairman of any premises within the area of theYatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha (here in after referred to as Pradeshiya Sabha)\n\n3. (2) The fee for a permit under this section shall be the fee charged by the Council in accordance with the provisionsof the Basic Law.\n\n(A)A person licensed under this by-law shall display his name and a plaque labeled \"Licensed Meat Shop\"and the current year's license in such a manner as to be easily visible on his premises.\n\n(B)Every meat shop shall display a Sinhala, Tamil and English copy of this by-law in a public and visibleplace."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_extraordinary_gazettes_2010s",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-05-2019-12-05-2152-58-en",
    "num": "2019-12-05-2152-58-en",
    "date_str": "2019-12-05",
    "description": "Sabaragamuwa  Provincial Council   -  By-Laws of  Ytiyanthota   Pradeshiya  Sabha",
    "url_metadata": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/extra-gazettes/egz_2019.html",
    "lang": "en",
    "url_pdf": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/extra-gazettes/2019/12/2152-58_E.pdf",
    "doc_number": "2152/58",
    "chunk_id": "2019-12-05-2019-12-05-2152-58-en-0106",
    "chunk_index": 106,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "4eb14304eb7b00cd7489d30471d62ce2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1971,
    "chunk_text": "(A)A person licensed under this by-law shall display his name and a plaque labeled \"Licensed Meat Shop\"and the current year's license in such a manner as to be easily visible on his premises.\n\n(B)Every meat shop shall display a Sinhala, Tamil and English copy of this by-law in a public and visibleplace.\n\n4. (1) The construction of the premises relevant to the permit shall be construed in accordance with the applicablewritten law and approved by the Chairman.\n\n4. (2) The organisms shall not rely on all equipment for storing, displaying, and selling meat, and shall not transmitfood inappropriate from the equipment used.\n\n4. (3) The bulbs and fixtures hanging above the meat for sale must be in safety condition and covered.\n\n4. (4) The floor shall be made of waterproof, non-absorbent, washable and non-slippery material without fine openingand shall be easy to clean and disinfect. There should be sufficient slope to allow the liquid to flow from the exit points of the ground.\n\n4. (5) The walls shall be made of waterproof, non-absorbent and washable material and shall be free of holes andinsects. The walls should be smooth to the height of the operation and should not have delicate openings. They should also be easy to clean and disinfect.\n\n62 A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\n4. (6) Surfaces directly in contact, with meat shall be of good quality, durable and easy to clean, maintain, anddisinfect. These surfaces should be made of materials that are smooth and non-absorbent and that the surfaces should be free from food, washing and disinfection.\n\n4. (7) The ceiling must be designed, constructed and finished to prevent the accumulation of dirt, to minimizecondensation and to prevent the molding and cracking of the ceiling."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_extraordinary_gazettes_2010s",
