    "chunk_text": "Date:- ......................................, Signature of the applicant. N.B :- If the place is a public place in the event of a free delivery or presentation of the above, a letter of consent from\n\nthe relevant institution or guardian or the owner of the place should be attached with the application.\n\n12-652/8\n\nAYAGAMA PRADESHIYA SABHA\n\nBy- Law Regarding Private Wells\n\nTHIS is to notify that I, Dhamma Dissanayake, Governor of the Sabaragamuwa Province has approved the By-law regarding private wells within authoritative area of Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha, prepared by the Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha by virtue of powers vested in it under Section 122 read with Section 126 of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, No. 15 of 1987 and passed at its General meeting held on 18.06.2019, by virtue of powers vested under Section 123(1) of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, read with Section 2 of Provincial Council (Consequential Provisions) Act, No. 12 of 1989, and it will be effective within authoritative area of Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha from the date this notification is published in the Gazette. DHAMMA DISSANAYAKE, Governor, Sabaragamuwa Province. At the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council, On this 30th day of October, 2019.\n\nBy-law on private wells in Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area\n\n1. This by-law is enacted to regulate private wells, including the prescribing of standards for the maintenance of the\n\nwells for regulatory purposes, to maintain the public health and safety of private wells maintained within the area of authority of Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n2. This by-law is known as the by-law of the private wells of Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n3. No individual well shall be constructed in the authoritative area of Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha (hearing after refer to\n\nas the area) to get water for drinking or other purpose except as otherwise specified under a plan approved by the Chairman for construction under the plan for construction of all private wells."
