    "md5": "10f34cd6ca61e2d1a5ebda61c752f4de",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1964,
    "chunk_text": "(I) The following Persons are entitled to be appointed to the Panel of a particular Special Mediation Board Area whosenames may be so submitted for appointment. A person eligible to be appointed as a Member of the Panel ofMediators in respect of the Special Mediation Board shall;\n\n(a) be between 35 to 70 years of age;\n\n(b) be a resident of the Special Mediation Board area;\n\n(c) have a professional or academic qualification obtained from a recognized professional or higher educationbody established by or under any written law; and\n\n(d) have been or be a public officer, or a person who holds knowledge and skills in an area relevant to settlementsof disputes and grievances of migrant workers.\n\n(I) (A)The following Individuals are entitled to submit nominations other than themselves for appointment to thePanel of a particular Special Mediation Board area:\n\n(i) A Public Officer or a Provincial Public Officer serving as the Head of a Department or as the RegionalHead of a Department in an office located within the Administrative District at which that particularSpecial Mediation Board area is situated:\n\n(ii) A Head of a Place or religious worship or of school situated in that particular Special Mediation Boardarea;\n\n(iii) A retired Head of a Department or School principal residing in that particular Special Mediation Boardarea;\n\n(B)Any board, Organizations or Institution which has been in existence at least for a period of five years andwhich is engaged in carrying out or doing anyone or more of the under mentioned objectives;\n\n(i)The enhancement of educational, religious, moral or spiritual, advancement of the community\n\n(ii)The enhancement of social welfare and eradication of poverty\n\n(iii)The enhancement of rural or community development.\n\n(iv)The enhancement of culture of sports\n\n(v)The enhancement of projects, programmes and activities intending providing and supplying basicneeds of the peoples such as health, food and shelter etc."
  },
